  "description": "Win32-native replacements for the Windows Forms controls that screen readers handle poorly. Menu bars and context menus built on real HMENU handles instead of WinForms' managed ToolStrip, announced as menu bars, submenus and popup menus, with mnemonic-collision validation and a proper accelerator table. Plus a ListView that screen readers can read past the first column, which the stock control's UI Automation provider prevents.",
